Usage: marbor nodes [action] [args] [flags]

Actions:
  confirm-tls <node>  pin a marbor agent's TLS certificate fingerprint (headless enrollment)
  patch <node>        update a node's deployment/placement fields (url, runtime, GPU, VRAM, parallelism, replica membership, TLS pin clear)
  tls-probe <node>    read a node's Marbor Agent TLS certificate fingerprint without pinning it
  add <name> <url>    add (or update, by name) a node in the fleet
  remove <node>       remove a node from the fleet
  warmup              get or set a node's proactive warmup config
  pinned              get or set a node's never-evict (pinned) model list
  prewarm             disable or re-enable predictive prewarm for a node
  fit                 show per-node VRAM fit analysis for resident/warm models
  suggestions         list multi-host replica groups detected from agent launch details, and confirm or dismiss them

Flags:
  --signal string    only nodes matching any of these signals, comma-separated or repeated: healthy, degraded, draining, down, agent, warm, pressure
  --search string    only nodes whose name or GPU model contains this text (trimmed, case-insensitive)
  --server string    Admin API base URL (default "http://localhost:8080", env MARBOR_SERVER)
  --json             output machine-readable JSON instead of a human table
  --username string  admin username, used to log in (env MARBOR_USERNAME)
  --password string  admin password, used to log in (env MARBOR_PASSWORD)

With --signal, lists only nodes that match any of the given signals, the same ones as the dashboard's filter chips: healthy,
degraded, draining, down, agent, warm, pressure. healthy and degraded leave out draining nodes; a node that is down and draining
matches both down and draining; agent means a live marbor agent is reporting; warm means a model is loaded; pressure means used
VRAM is at least 90% of a known total (a node without measured VRAM never matches, so "no pressure" there means unknown, not ok).
--search keeps nodes whose name or GPU model contains the text, trimmed and ignoring case, and combines with --signal. Giving --signal more
than once adds to the list. No match is an empty table (header only) or [] with --json and still exits 0, so scripts that act on
matches should count rows rather than check the exit status.

requires credentials: run "marbor login" once (recommended), or pass --username+--password (or MARBOR_USERNAME+MARBOR_PASSWORD).
